ll}, {"id": "661f51_p3", "source_url": "https://stackoverflow.com/questions/23351796/django-block-internet-connection-for-testing-purposes", "source_title": "python - Django: block internet connection for testing purposes - Stack Overflow", "text": "I'd like to make sure my unit tests do not try to connect to Internet, is there a way to raise an exception when they do?\nThere was a similar question [Python: block network connections for testing purposes?](https://stackoverflow.com/questions/18601828/python-block-network-connections-for-testing-purposes), but the solution proposed there blocks all socket connections, including the database ones, which is not acceptable for Django tests.\n\n- [python](/questions/tagged/python)\n- [django](/questions/tagged/django)\n- [unit-testing](/questions/tagged/unit-testing)\n- [testing](/questions/tagged/testing)\n\n[Share](/q/23351796)\n[Improve this question](/posts/23351796/edit)\n\n[edited May 23, 2017 at 11:45](/posts/23351796/revisions)\n\n[Community](/users/-1/community)Bot\n111 silver badge\n\n[Ivan Ivanov](/users/905318/ivan-ivanov)\n2,08211 gold badge1919 silver badges3030 bronze badges2\n\npossible duplicate of [How can I disable a third party API when executing Django unit tests?](http://stackoverflow.com/questions/3730286/how-can-i-disable-a-third-party-api-when-executing-django-unit-tests)", "char_start": null, "char_end": null, "corpus_id": null}, {"id": "661f51_p4", "source_url": "https://stackoverflow.com/questions/23351796/django-block-internet-connection-for-testing-purposes", "source_title": "python - Django: block internet connection for testing purposes - Stack Overflow", "text": "Brad Beattie\n–\n                        [Brad Beattie](/users/183948/brad-beattie)\n2014-04-28 23:21:02 +00:00CommentedApr 28, 2014 at 23:21\n\n@BradBeattie definitely not, that question is about mocking API calls, I just want to make sure I have mocked everything that connects to the Internet and didn't miss a thing (I want the tests to fail otherwise)\n\nIvan Ivanov\n–\n                        [Ivan Ivanov](/users/905318/ivan-ivanov)\n2014-04-28 23:56:14 +00:00CommentedApr 28, 2014 at 23:56\n[\n                        Add a comment\n                    ](#) |\n\n##\n3 Answers                                        3\n\nSorted by:\n        [\n            Reset to default\n        ](/questions/23351796/django-block-internet-connection-for-testing-purposes?answertab=scoredesc#tab-top)\n\nFound out a way to do this. You can paste this into your settings.if 'test' in sys.argv:\n\n# Block Internet access during tests\n    import urllib2\n    import httplib\n    import httplib2\n\ndef _raise_http_error(*args, **kwargs):\n        raise urllib2.URLError(\"I told you not to use the Internet!\")", "char_start": null, "char_end": null, "corpus_id": null}, {"id": "661f51_p5", "source_url": "https://stackoverflow.com/questions/23351796/django-block-internet-connection-for-testing-purposes", "source_title": "python - Django: block internet connection for testing purposes - Stack Overflow", "text": "class AngryHandler(urllib2.BaseHandler):\n        handler_order = 1\n\ndef default_open(self, req):\n            _raise_http_error()\n\nopener = urllib2.build_opener(AngryHandler)\n    urllib2.install_opener(opener)\n\n_HTTPHandler = urllib2.HTTPHandler\n    urllib2.HTTPHandler = AngryHandler\n\nhttplib.HTTPConnection.connect = lambda self: None\n    httplib.HTTPSConnection.connect = lambda self: None\n    httplib.HTTPConnection.request = _raise_http_error\n    httplib.HTTPSConnection.request = _raise_http_error\n    httplib2.Http.request = _raise_http_error\n\n[Share](/a/23378791)\n[Improve this answer](/posts/23378791/edit)\n\n[edited May 26, 2017 at 17:10](/posts/23378791/revisions)\n\n[Ivan Ivanov](/users/905318/ivan-ivanov)\n2,08211 gold badge1919 silver badges3030 bronze badges\n\nSign up to request clarification or add additional context in comments.\n\nmlissner\n[mlissner](/users/64911/mlissner) [Over a year ago](#comment63115735_23378791)", "char_start": null, "char_end": null, "corpus_id": null}, {"id": "661f51_p6", "source_url": "https://stackoverflow.com/questions/23351796/django-block-internet-connection-for-testing-purposes", "source_title": "python - Django: block internet connection for testing purposes - Stack Overflow", "text": "Seems easier to block socket, which I think is upstream of all of these libraries. There's an example here that seems to do something like that: [stackoverflow.com/a/18601897/64911](http://stackoverflow.com/a/18601897/64911) 2016-06-15T05:00:12.257Z+00:00\n\nTake a look at vcrpy: [https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy](https://github.com/kevin1024/vcrpy)\nThe first time you run the test it'll make the external request. Every time after that it'll use a fixture that it stored from the first call. The external requests never get made again, which is what you're trying to accomplish.\nUsage is dead simple using a decorator on your unit test:@vcr.use_cassette('fixtures/vcr_cassettes/synopsis.yaml')\ndef test_iana():\n    response = urllib2.urlopen('http://www.iana.org/domains/reserved').read()\n    assert 'Example domains' in response\n\nSupports any request made using the following libraries:\n- urllib2\n- urllib3\n- http.client (python3)\n- requests (both 1.x and 2.x\nversions)\n- httplib2\n- boto\n- Tornado’s AsyncHTTPClient\n\n[Share](/a/34831181)\n[Improve this answer](/posts/34831181/edit)", "char_start": null, "char_end": null, "corpus_id": null}, {"id": "661f51_p7", "source_url": "https://stackoverflow.com/questions/23351796/django-block-internet-connection-for-testing-purposes", "source_title": "python - Django: block internet connection for testing purposes - Stack Overflow", "text": "[MNM](/users/420678/mnm)\n2,18911 gold badge1313 silver badges1313 bronze badges\n\n[httpretty](https://github.com/gabrielfalcao/HTTPretty) solves this problem.\nWrite a custom test runner where you disable only 3rd party API calls, only in your test suite.# common/test_runner.py\n\nimport httpretty\nfrom django.test.runner import DiscoverRunner\n\nclass CustomTestRunner(DiscoverRunner):\n    def run_tests(self, *args, **kwargs):\n        with httpretty.enabled(allow_net_connect=False):\n            return super().run_tests(*args, **kwargs)\n\nadd this new test runner to your settingsTEST_RUNNER = \"common.test_runner.CustomTestRunner\"\n\nAnd from now on all external API calls have to be mocked or httpretty.errors.UnmockedError will be raised.\nAlternatively, if your project uses [responses](https://github.com/getsentry/responses) library, responses.activate or responses.start should work similarly.\n\n[Share](/a/68838903)\n[Improve this answer](/posts/68838903/edit)\n\n[edited Jan 28, 2022 at 11:49](/posts/68838903/revisions)", "char_start": null, "char_end": null, "corpus_id": null}, {"id": "661f51_p8", "source_url": "https://stackoverflow.com/questions/23351796/django-block-internet-connection-for-testing-purposes", "source_title": "python - Django: block internet connection for testing purposes - Stack Overflow", "text": "[Tom Wojcik](/users/5833429/tom-wojcik)\n6,30944 gold badges3939 silver badges5555 bronze badges\n\n##\n                                        Your Answer\n\nThanks for contributing an answer to Stack Overflow!\n- Please be sure to answer the question. Provide details and share your research!\nBut avoid …\n- Asking for help, clarification, or responding to other answers.\n- Making statements based on opinion; back them up with references or personal experience.\nTo learn more, see our [tips on writing great answers](/help/how-to-answer).\n\n### Sign up or [log in](/users/login?ssrc=question_page&returnurl=https%3a%2f%2fstackoverflow.com%2fquestions%2f23351796%2fdjango-block-internet-connection-for-testing-purposes%23new-answer)\n\nSign up using Email and Password\n                        Submit\n\nBy clicking “Post Your Answer”, you agree to our [terms of service](https://stackoverflow.com/legal/terms-of-service/public) and acknowledge you have read our [privacy policy](https://stackoverflow.com/legal/privacy-policy).", "char_start": null, "char_end": null, "corpus_id": null}, {"id": "661f51_p9", "source_url": "https://stackoverflow.com/questions/23351796/django-block-internet-connection-for-testing-purposes", "source_title": "python - Django: block internet connection for testing purposes - Stack Overflow", "text": "Start asking to get answers\nFind the answer to your question by asking.[Ask question](/questions/ask)\n\n- [python](/questions/tagged/python)\n- [django](/questions/tagged/django)\n- [unit-testing](/questions/tagged/unit-testing)\n- [testing](/questions/tagged/testing)\nSee similar questions with these tags.\n\n[Making the OWASP top ten in the vibe code...](https://stackoverflow.blog/2026/06/05/making-the-owasp-top-ten-in-the-vibe-code-era/)\n                            Featured on Meta\n\n[Native Ads Coming To Comments](https://meta.stackexchange.com/questions/418563/native-ads-coming-to-comments)\n\n[Policy: Generative AI (e.g., ChatGPT) is banned](https://meta.stackoverflow.com/questions/421831/policy-generative-ai-e-g-chatgpt-is-banned)\n\n[Help Shape the 2026 Developer Survey!](https://meta.stackoverflow.com/questions/438884/help-shape-the-2026-developer-survey)", "char_start": null, "char_end": null, "corpus_id": null}, {"id": "661f51_p10", "source_url": "https://stackoverflow.com/questions/23351796/django-block-internet-connection-for-testing-purposes", "source_title": "python - Django: block internet connection for testing purposes - Stack Overflow", "text": "[\n52](/questions/18601828/python-block-network-connections-for-testing-purposes)[Python: block network connections for testing purposes?](/questions/18601828/python-block-network-connections-for-testing-purposes?noredirect=1)\n[\n4](/questions/3730286/how-can-i-disable-a-third-party-api-when-executing-django-unit-tests)[How can I disable a third party API when exec