103-# ---- progress-aware terminal-wait sentinels (Bug 15) ------------------------
104-# The terminal wait is PROGRESS-AWARE, not a blind wall-clock: while the conversation
105-# is still emitting NEW events (max seq / event count advancing) or its status is
106-# actively transitioning, we KEEP WAITING. A wall-clock cutoff only ends the wait when
107-# the run is GENUINELY INACTIVE (no progress for the inactivity window) or a generous
108-# HARD CAP bounds a truly-hung run. The two timeout outcomes are NOT the same finding:
109-#   * PROGRESSING_TIMEOUT — the hard cap was hit while the build was STILL actively
110-#     progressing (events advanced within the inactivity window). The runner could NOT
111-#     obtain a terminal verdict; this is INCONCLUSIVE (model-speed / harness limitation),
112-#     NOT a product BUILD_DID_NOT_FINISH → the caller records INVALID_RUN so §17 re-runs it.
113-#   * INACTIVE_TIMEOUT — the build went genuinely SILENT (no new events) for the inactivity
114-#     window: a real wedge. The caller falls through to normal classification (the
115-#     collected non-terminal run is a genuine finding: BUILD_DID_NOT_FINISH / STUCK).
116-PROGRESSING_TIMEOUT = "PROGRESSING_TIMEOUT"
117-INACTIVE_TIMEOUT = "INACTIVE_TIMEOUT"
