120-# The runner sends each `after_terminal` follow-up as its own re-plan→approve→terminal
121-# cycle. The bug: the post-terminal poll returned IMMEDIATELY on the STALE prior FINISHED
122-# status, so follow-up 2 was sent before the engine even started processing follow-up 1;
123-# the engine then only processes the LATEST unprocessed user turn, COLLAPSING the piled-up
124-# follow-ups into ONE plan revision (rev 2 vs an expected 3) → false PLAN_REVISION_NOT_INCREMENTED.
125-# `wait_for_followup_pickup` blocks AFTER each send until the engine actually PICKS UP the
126-# follow-up (relative to a baseline captured BEFORE the send) so the follow-ups are serialized.
127-FOLLOWUP_PICKED_UP = "FOLLOWUP_PICKED_UP"  # the build left its prior terminal status (processing)
128-FOLLOWUP_REPLANNED = "FOLLOWUP_REPLANNED"  # a re-plan signal (planning re-entry / revision bump)
129-FOLLOWUP_PICKUP_TIMEOUT = "FOLLOWUP_PICKUP_TIMEOUT"  # no pickup within the bound → caller proceeds
130-# enter_planning stamps this status DETAIL on a re-plan re-entry (RUNNING + detail="planning");
